 *** WARNING! RKBIMPort ignored since no URKBAL
 * Print level:    0
 * Dirac-Coulomb Hamiltonian
 * Kohn-Sham calculation using the xc functional: LDA
 * SS integrals neglected:
   Interatomic Coulombic SS-contributions modelled by
   classical repulsion of small component atomic charges
   using tabulated charges.
 * Default integral flags passed to all modules
   - LL-integrals:     1
   - LS-integrals:     1
   - SS-integrals:     0
   - GT-integrals:     0
 * Basis set:
   - uncontracted large component basis set
   - uncontracted small component basis set


 Information about the restricted kinetic balance scheme:
 * Default RKB projection:
   1: Pre-projection in scalar basis
   2: Removal of unphysical solutions (via diagonalization of free particle Hamiltonian)
  
===========================================================================
  
  Frozen Density Embedding (FDE) Calculation setup
 
 * Print level                  :     0
 * Non-additive functional : (KE) kin_tf              
                             (XC) lda                 
 
   if .RSPLDA set will use : (XC) lda                 
                             (KE) kin_tf              
 
 * FDE Potential generated from frozen, active densities
 
   Embedding potential included according to:S. Hofener, A.S.P. Gomes and L. Visscher,
    J. Chem. Phys. 136 (2012) 044104.S. Hofener, A.S.P. Gomes and L. Visscher,
    J. Chem. Phys. 139 (2013) 104106.
 
  Frozen density integrates to        10.002906 electrons
  Grid points processed         4300
 * Density (and gradient) from frozen subsystems read from file: FROZEN                                                      
 
   Response contributions to the active subsystem,when included, are calculated according to:
   S. Hofener, A.S.P. Gomes and L. Visscher, J. Chem. Phys. 136 (2012) 044104.
   S. Hofener, A.S.P. Gomes and L. Visscher, J. Chem. Phys. 139 (2013) 104106.
 
===========================================================================
  
  ===== Kohn-Sham calculation set-up =====
 * DFT thresholds:
   - small density threshold =  0.10000E-13
 * Spin density contribution in response calculations:
   - use the norm of the spin magnetization vector as a definition of the spin density (noncollinear definition)
  ===== Numerical integration grid =====
   - integration grid imported from file numerical_grid                


